1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,200
This is how we keep score today:

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:05,009
one bead per goal, pushed by hand…

3
00:00:05,009 --> 00:00:08,836
After the match: a brief forensic investigation.

4
00:00:08,836 --> 00:00:12,356
Then someone types the result into the MMR app.

5
00:00:12,356 --> 00:00:13,876
With great confidence.

6
00:00:13,876 --> 00:00:15,743
And probably wrong.

7
00:00:15,743 --> 00:00:16,743
We're engineers.

8
00:00:16,743 --> 00:00:19,306
We can easily be lazier than this.

9
00:00:19,306 --> 00:00:22,506
So: a small box in each goal's ball drawer.

10
00:00:22,506 --> 00:00:24,106
Every single ball rolls

11
00:00:24,106 --> 00:00:26,321
through an infrared beam.

12
00:00:27,173 --> 00:00:29,413
The beam sits at the ball's centre.

13
00:00:29,413 --> 00:00:32,472
Even the saddest roll can't sneak past.

14
00:00:32,472 --> 00:00:34,072
Nobody has to watch.

15
00:00:34,072 --> 00:00:36,001
Nobody has to argue.

16
00:00:36,001 --> 00:00:40,481
Inside sits a tiny ESP32 that counts the balls.

17
00:00:40,481 --> 00:00:42,303
No AI involved.

18
00:00:42,303 --> 00:00:45,661
A motion sensor wakes it when the table moves.

19
00:00:45,661 --> 00:00:48,621
Plus an infrared LED, a light sensor,

20
00:00:48,621 --> 00:00:50,832
and three AA batteries.

21
00:00:50,832 --> 00:00:53,472
It all lives in a 3D-printed sled,

22
00:00:53,472 --> 00:00:54,752
in two halves.

23
00:00:54,752 --> 00:00:57,049
They go in where the balls come out.

24
00:00:57,049 --> 00:01:00,770
A slanted wall sends every ball past the beam.

25
00:01:00,770 --> 00:01:02,690
Every goal gets a little chirp.

26
00:01:02,690 --> 00:01:03,570
No chirp?

27
00:01:03,570 --> 00:01:05,195
Then it didn't count.

28
00:01:05,195 --> 00:01:06,875
Counted a hand by mistake?

29
00:01:06,875 --> 00:01:09,115
Hold the undo button for a second.

30
00:01:09,115 --> 00:01:09,755
Gone.

31
00:01:09,755 --> 00:01:11,355
You get ten seconds.

32
00:01:11,355 --> 00:01:14,014
After that, it's your phone's problem.

33
00:01:14,014 --> 00:01:15,214
When the table moves,

34
00:01:15,214 --> 00:01:17,774
it wakes and joins the Wi-Fi.

35
00:01:17,774 --> 00:01:20,700
Score, and the server knows instantly.

36
00:01:20,700 --> 00:01:22,620
The server does the bookkeeping.

37
00:01:22,620 --> 00:01:25,850
The device itself doesn't even know the score.

38
00:01:25,850 --> 00:01:27,530
Even the two goal counters

39
00:01:27,530 --> 00:01:30,410
on the same table never talk to each other.

40
00:01:30,410 --> 00:01:32,173
Only to the server.

41
00:01:32,173 --> 00:01:34,653
Someone yanks the batteries mid-match?

42
00:01:34,653 --> 00:01:37,313
Every goal is saved before it's sent.

43
00:01:37,313 --> 00:01:39,153
Three AA batteries.

44
00:01:39,153 --> 00:01:40,273
By our estimate,

45
00:01:40,273 --> 00:01:42,433
a set lasts about one and a half

46
00:01:42,433 --> 00:01:44,527
to three and a half months.

47
00:01:44,527 --> 00:01:47,997
Only the motion sensor isn't allowed to sleep.

48
00:01:47,997 --> 00:01:48,877
After the match,

49
00:01:48,877 --> 00:01:50,797
the app already knows the score.

50
00:01:50,797 --> 00:01:52,580
You just tap.

51
00:01:53,463 --> 00:01:56,270
Was any of this strictly necessary?

52
00:01:56,270 --> 00:01:58,097
Nooope.

53
00:01:58,827 --> 00:02:01,004
Because we're lazy.

54
00:02:01,161 --> 00:02:03,546
And because we can.
